fix(generate-docs): resolve the repository root, not $PWD and not the cwd

Three defects, all in the same lookup, and all introduced by the commit that
ported docgen's README/AGENTS marker rewriting.

1. It read `$PWD` straight out of the environment with no check. Go's os.Getwd
   only trusts PWD when it names the current directory (os/getwd.go). A stale
   PWD therefore sent the README lookup into an unrelated tree, and the command
   failed with a path error naming a place the caller never ran.

2. `go_working_dir` compared the two `canonicalize` Results directly, so when
   BOTH calls failed, `None == None` read as "they match" and the stale path was
   returned. Both sides must resolve, and then be equal.

3. It then used the working directory directly. Go resolves its own root, and
   so must this: `cargo test` runs a test binary with the PACKAGE directory as
   its working directory, so the README lookup landed in crates/bv and failed
   even though the repository has a README.

`repo_root()` walks up to the nearest ancestor holding `.git`, which is what
the test needed and what Go does.

I reported this one wrong in the previous turn: I called it an artefact of the
shell's working directory being stuck in a fixture and did not measure it. It
reproduced from the repository root, and cargo test was correctly red. Measuring
is what found all three.

Verified with an installed binary (cargo install --root /tmp/bvri, since
~/.local/bin is on the sealed read-only volume):

  --generate-docs from the repo root   exit 0
  cargo test --workspace               0 failures
  cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings   clean
  tmp/verify.py                        29 differ, 19 clean (unchanged)

